Iris Flower Classification using Machine Learning
This project predicts the species of an Iris flower based on its sepal and petal dimensions using supervised machine learning.

🔍 Problem Statement
Given measurements of an Iris flower — sepal length, sepal width, petal length, and petal width — predict its species:

Setosa

Versicolor

Virginica

Project Structure

IrisFlowerClassification/
├── iris_app.py         ← Streamlit application
├── requirements.txt    ← Project dependencies
└── README.md           ← Project documentation


📊 Dataset
Source: scikit-learn’s built-in Iris dataset

Samples: 150 flowers

Features:

Sepal Length (cm)

Sepal Width (cm)

Petal Length (cm)

Petal Width (cm)

Target: Species (Setosa, Versicolor, Virginica)

🧠 What the App Does
Takes user input for flower dimensions via sliders

Uses a trained Logistic Regression model to predict species

Displays the result in a user-friendly format

📦 Technologies Used
Category	Tools
Language	Python
Libraries	scikit-learn, pandas, numpy
Interface	Streamlit
Deployment	Streamlit Community Cloud

📈 Accuracy
Achieved 100% accuracy on a test split using LogisticRegression, due to the clean and separable nature of the Iris dataset.

💡 Future Improvements
Add support for multiple classifiers (KNN, Decision Tree)

Visualize decision boundaries

Upload CSV input for batch predictions

Deploy on other platforms (like Hugging Face Spaces)

